  "previous_increment": "doc/validation/bounded-host-metadata-2026-09-13.json",
  "behavior": [
    "Hybrid fixed roles use a private sorted exact-size box, preserving absent values, checked unique roles, shallow native aliases for ordinary checkpoints and independent option slots.",
    "Prepared leaves borrow original operands with no descriptor cloning, view creation, metadata query or native work during visitation. Copy and retained-copy workers consume the same slots.",
    "Concat copies padded key/value slots; compressed copies logical latent/rotary views into independent compact storage with capacity equal to length; pooling preserves all five optional slots and scalar controls.",
    "Closed pooling-attention composition preserves local, primary and optional index stream ordering without architecture-family dispatch or new host containers.",
    "Each actual copy uses the existing Contiguous(false)/DeepCopy program. Recovery collectors retain produced intermediates and final outputs before later fallible work, with alias-retirement and injected between-slot failure coverage.",
    "Source aliases retain separate destination slots. Compressed retained-state traversal now includes padded stores when checkpoint cloning gave them independent backing, while copy operands remain the two logical views.",
    "Prepared resident compressed and pooling-attention programs reject paged storage before native work; existing paged isolated-snapshot paths retain their prior manager-copy behavior."
  ],
  "initial_findings": [
    "Two private semantic-transaction tests still used BTreeMap read APIs after fixed-role migration; converted to the existing iterator/component contracts.",
    "Two initial targeted filters selected zero tests; their logs are retained and excluded from final validation. The final runner rejects empty selections.",
    "Independent review found an immediate native-owner retirement assumption in the new fixed-copy failure test; corrected to explicit reclamation before final validation.",
    "Independent review narrowed the pooling-attention prepared enum into an opaque struct so callers cannot assemble unrelated source variants.",
    "Independent review exposed preexisting compressed source traversal omitting detached padded stores; corrected and covered by a nonzero physical-inventory regression.",
    "The added inventory test initially imported RetainedStorage from its parent instead of storage module; corrected before successful final build.",
    "An existing prediction snapshot test equated all retained backing with its two logical numerical arrays; separated logical parity from complete backing-independence assertions after traversal was corrected."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Copy leaves do not confer allocation permission or whole-state funding. Complete source inventory and destination operands are separate; source roots not copied must remain independently authenticated and pinned.",
    "Exact retained fixed-role box capacity excludes enclosing mutable state/layer payload, arbitrary iterator construction scratch, recovery collector capacity, allocator metadata and process/system memory.",
    "Whole native snapshots still need actual mutable host source bootstrap, closed host destination construction, one combined decoder/sampler account and an immutable saved decoder owner.",
    "Paged catalogs, transfers, independent namespace publication and recovery remain separate unfinished whole-copy mechanisms.",
    "Complete facade parser/controller, decoder, capture and delivery accounting and fresh resumed-run admission remain unfinished. The whole finite snapshot guard stays.",
    "No new released-checkpoint, distributed numerical, hardware or process/allocator-peak measurement was performed. Full family/path bounded inference remains incomplete."
  ]
}
